    "finding": "E1's spearman() ranks with np.argsort(np.argsort(x)), which breaks ties by ARRAY POSITION instead of averaging them. The harmful refusal rate has a TIE: 2 of the 4 members share the value 0.000 (qwen3-0.6b/abliterated and smollm2/base). The reported rho = -0.20 is therefore an artefact of the alphabetical order in which those two tied members happen to sit; with conventional average ranks the same data give rho = +0.105, a SIGN FLIP. This is a second, independent reason the -0.20 cannot carry a directional claim, on top of the n = 4 power floor."
  },
