  "corrected_claim_text": "On this four-model panel SPI did not order the models by measured harmful refusal rate (Spearman rho = -0.20, exact two-sided p = 1.000 over all 4! = 24 orderings). The two supervised baselines ordered it no better than chance either (diff-in-means AUROC rho = 0.40, p = 0.667; r_0 margin rho = 0.40, p = 0.750). The smallest two-sided p attainable at n = 4 is 0.4167 (one-sided 0.1667), so NO result on this panel - a perfect ordering included - could reach 0.05 two-sided. Moreover only 1 of 4 members sits above the refusal / incapacity floor, so a rank correlation here is an instruct-vs-rest contrast, not a graded ranking. Two of the four members are TIED at a refusal rate of 0.000, and the -0.20 is produced by a rank function that breaks that tie by array position; with average ranks the same data give rho = +0.11. No ordering claim, in either direction, is supported at this panel size.",
